- Description: 1857 overland mail route established by John Butterfield, sweeping across the southern U.S.; stagecoaches carried passengers, freight, and mail.
- Activities: Not listed.
- Weather: Varies widely along route; check local forecasts (weather.gov).
- Location: 32.2768237589, -106.796583304
- Entrance Fees: None listed.
- Operating Hours: Not a single marked hiking trail; a corridor across mixed ownership, including private lands. Access/hours vary by site; contact sites before visiting. Standard hours: All day, daily.
- Contacts: Email ntir_information@nps.gov

Cabrillo National Monument (code: cabr) — CA
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/cabr/index.htm
- Designation: National Monument
- Description: Commemorates Juan Rodríguez Cabrillo’s 1542 landing on the West Coast; rich cultural and natural resources.
- Activities: Biking/Road Biking; Hiking; Living History; Reenactments; Historic Weapons Demonstrations; First-Person Interpretation; Junior Ranger; Wildlife/Birdwatching; Park Film; Museum Exhibits; Shopping/Bookstore; Gift Shop/Souvenirs.
- Weather: Mild year-round San Diego climate; warm, dry summers; mild winters; most rain Dec–Mar; 201+ days above 70°F; 9–13 in annual rainfall. Check NWS (weather.gov).
- Location: 32.6722503, -117.2415985
- Entrance Fees:
  - Private Vehicle $20: admits one private non-commercial vehicle + passengers.
  - Motorcycle $15.
  - Per Person $10 (walk-in/bike); up to 4 people capped at $20; ages ≤15 free.
  - Commercial: Sedan $30 (1–6); Van $45 (7–25); Mini-bus $45 (7–25); Motor Coach $100 (26+).
  - Organized Non-Commercial Groups: Vehicles ≤16 seats pay $20 vehicle fee; ≥17 seats pay $10 per non-free individual; max $100 per vehicle.
- Operating Hours: Open daily, 9 AM–5 PM (including holidays). Bayside & Oceanside Trails close 4 PM; tidepools & Coastal Trail close 4:30 PM.
- Contacts: Phone 619-523-4285; Email cabr_info@nps.gov

California National Historic Trail (code: cali) — CA, CO, ID, KS, MO, NE, NV, OR, UT, WY
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/cali/index.htm
- Designation: National Historic Trail
- Description: 5,000+ miles across 10 states; followed by 250,000+ emigrants to California’s gold fields and farmlands in the 1840s–50s; 1,000+ miles of wagon ruts/traces remain.
- Activities: Auto/ATV Scenic Driving; Self-guided Auto Tours; Guided Tours; Hiking; Horseback Riding/Horse Trekking; Junior Ranger; Museum Exhibits.
- Weather: Varies widely; check local forecasts (weather.gov).
- Location: 42.3999643979, -108.702415369
- Entrance Fees: None listed.
- Operating Hours: Corridor across communities, public lands, and private property; access/hours vary by site. Standard hours: All day, daily.
- Contacts: Email ntir_information@nps.gov

