Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'cabr'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 1699 tokens): SUMMARIZED CONTENT:
- Name: Cabrillo National Monument (code: cabr)
- Designation: National Monument
- State: CA
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/cabr/index.htm
- Description: In 1542, Juan Rodriguez Cabrillo became the first European to set foot on the U.S. West Coast. The monument tells this exploration story and preserves rich cultural and natural resources. “Embark on your own Voyage of Exploration.”

Location
- Address: 1800 Cabrillo Memorial Drive, San Diego, CA 92106
- Coordinates: 32.6722503, -117.2415985

Directions
- From downtown San Diego: Harbor Dr past the airport → Left on Rosecrans St → Right on Canon St → Left on Catalina Blvd (Cabrillo Memorial Dr) → Follow to the end
- Directions info: https://www.nps.gov/cabr/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Weather
- Check current weather: https://www.weather.gov/
- Climate: Warm, dry summers; mild winters. Most rain Dec–Mar. ~201 days/year above 70 °F (21 °C). Annual rainfall ~9–13 inches (230–330 mm).

Contacts
- Phone: 619-523-4285
- Email: cabr_info@nps.gov

Entrance Fees
- Entrance – Private Vehicle: $20.00; admits one private, non-commercial vehicle and passengers.
- Entrance – Motorcycle: $15.00; admits one motorcycle and passenger(s).
- Entrance – Per Person: $10.00; for entry by foot/bicycle. Groups up to 4 walking/biking capped at $20 total. Ages 15 and under free.
- Commercial Entrance – Sedan: $30.00; capacity 1–6.
- Commercial Entrance – Van: $45.00; capacity 7–25.
- Commercial Entrance – Mini-bus: $45.00; capacity 7–25.
- Commercial Entrance – Motor Coach: $100.00; capacity 26+.
- Entrance – Non-commercial Groups: $20.00 per vehicle (capacity ≤16). For vehicles with 17+ seats: $10 per non-free passenger; max $100 per vehicle.

Entrance Passes
- None listed.

Operating Hours
- Open daily, 365 days/year: 9 am–5 pm.
- Trail/area closures: Bayside Trail and Oceanside Trail close at 4 pm; tidepools and Coastal Trail close at 4:30 pm.
- Standard hours (daily): 9:00AM–5:00PM.

Topics
- Burial, Cemetery and Gravesite; National Cemetery; Explorers and Expeditions; Maritime; Coastal Defenses; Maritime – Military; Lighthouses; Ships and Shipwrecks; Military; Monuments and Memorials; Animals; Birds; Oceans; Whales; Scenic Views.

Activities
- Biking; Road Biking; Hiking; Living History; Reenactments; Historic Weapons Demonstration; First Person Interpretation; Junior Ranger Program; Wildlife Watching; Birdwatching; Park Film; Museum Exhibits; Shopping; Bookstore and Park Store; Gift Shop and Souvenirs.

