Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'goga'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 3048 tokens): - Name: Golden Gate National Recreation Area (code: goga)
- Designation: National Recreation Area
- State: CA
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/goga/index.htm
- Description: Urban coastal park with 19 ecosystems and 2,000+ plant/animal species. Hike, enjoy vistas, picnic, and explore layered history from Indigenous cultures through Spanish colonialism, Mexican Republic, U.S. military expansion, and San Francisco’s growth.
- Weather: Winters are cool with sporadic rain and sunny breaks; grasses green. Blooms start late Feb–Mar through May–Jun. By July, summer fog dominates coastal areas; vegetation turns golden brown/gray. Sept–Oct are typically clear and sunny park-wide.
- Directions: Sites span 60+ miles north/south of San Francisco, mainly along the coast. Access via Highways 1, 101, 280 (North/South Bay) and I-80 (East Bay). Park HQ (Fort Mason) entrance at Franklin & Bay Sts., San Francisco. More: http://www.nps.gov/goga/planyourvisit/directions.htm
- Location: 37.85982543, -122.6007386; Address: Golden Gate National Recreation Area, 201 Fort Mason, San Francisco, CA 94123
- Contacts: Phone 415-561-4700; Email goga_socialmedia_goga@nps.gov
- Entrance fees/passes: None listed
- Operating hours:
  - Parking Lots: Urban park generally accessible 24/7 in most areas; most parking lots open sunrise–sunset.
  - Day Use Areas (6 a.m.–1 hour after sunset):
    - Marin County: Conzelman Rd (west, between traffic circle and Field Rd.), Kirby Cove (except permitted campers), Muir Beach, Muir Beach Overlook, Stinson Beach.
