  - On Sokoban, Maze, and Taxi, WMAct turns multi-turn tasks into single-turn successes, improves transfer to harder environments, and boosts performance on reasoning benchmarks.

- 2511.23474v1 — A Lyapunov-Based Small-Gain Theorem for Fixed-Time Stability (eess.SY, 2025-11-28)
  - Develops a Lyapunov-based nonlinear small-gain theorem guaranteeing fixed-time stability (FxTS) for interconnected systems when each subsystem admits a fixed-time ISS Lyapunov function (FxT-ISS).
  - Extends small-gain results known for asymptotic and finite-time stability to the fixed-time setting, filling a theoretical gap.
  - Demonstrated via analytical/numerical examples, including fixed-time feedback optimization without plant–controller time-scale separation.

- 2511.23473v1 — ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems (cs.LG/cs.CL, 2025-11-28)
  - Open-source evolution framework that unifies in-context learning and reinforcement learning at test time to improve bounds on open problems, simplifying and extending AlphaEvolve to a single LLM.
  - Features: large program database for exploration, batch sampling for throughput, lazy penalties to avoid stagnation, optional reward shaping for stable training.
  - A small open-source model (DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B) achieves new best-known bounds on circle packing and the first autocorrelation inequality.
  - Across two models and four open tasks, test-time RL consistently outperforms inference-only; RL-trained checkpoints progress faster and generalize better. Code: https://github.com/ypwang61/ThetaEvolve

