4) AnyTalker: Scaling Multi-Person Talking Video Generation (cs.CV; 2025-11-28)
- Problem: Audio-driven multi-person generation is hampered by data scarcity and coherent multi-identity control.
- Method: Extensible multi-stream architecture with identity-aware attention in a Diffusion Transformer; iteratively processes identity–audio pairs for arbitrary identity scaling.
- Training: Learns multi-person patterns from single-person videos; refines interactivity with a small set of real multi-person clips.
- Contributions: New metric and dataset for evaluating naturalness/interactivity.
- Results: Strong lip sync, visual quality, and natural interactivity; balances data cost with identity scalability.

5) Lyapunov-Based Small-Gain Theorem for Fixed-Time Stability (eess.SY; 2025-11-28)
- Problem: Gap in fixed-time stability (FxTS) guarantees for interconnected systems.
- Method: If each subsystem has a fixed-time ISS Lyapunov function (FxT-ISS) and a nonlinear small-gain condition holds, the interconnected system is FxTS.
- Significance: Lyapunov-based small-gain theory for FxTS analogous to asymptotic/finite-time results.
- Examples: Analytical/numerical demos, including fixed-time feedback optimization without time-scale separation.

6) ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems (cs.LG; cs.CL; 2025-11-28)
- Goal: Open-source framework extending AlphaEvolve for evolving programmatic solutions with a single LLM that continues learning at test time via RL.
- Features: Large program database, batch sampling, lazy penalties, reward shaping; efficient scaling of in-context + RL at test time.
- Results: A small open-source model (DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B) achieves new best-known bounds on circle packing and the first auto-correlation inequality;
