  - Covers regulation of decorative lenses and artificial tears, compares US vs international approaches, and anticipates AI-dr
Tool `Paper Search:search_arxiv` with Parameter {'query': 'foundation models in healthcare 2024', 'max_results': 10} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 4699 tokens): - Video-R2: Reinforcing Consistent and Grounded Reasoning in Multimodal Language Models (cs.CV; 2025-11-28)
  - Authors: Muhammad Maaz; Hanoona Rasheed; Fahad Shahbaz Khan; Salman Khan
  - Problem: Video reasoning traces from MLLMs can be convincing yet logically inconsistent or weakly grounded in visual evidence; models often lean on linguistic priors.
  - Contributions:
    - Diagnostic metrics: Think–Answer Consistency (TAC) for alignment between reasoning and answers; Video Attention Score (VAS) for reliance on visual vs textual cues.
    - Post-training: timestamp-aware SFT + Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) with a new Temporal Alignment Reward (TAR) to enforce temporal precision and causal coherence.
  - Results: Higher TAC, VAS, and accuracy across 11 video reasoning benchmarks; improved temporal alignment yields more accurate, trustworthy video understanding.
  - Resources: Code, dataset, and model to be open-sourced. PDF: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.23478v1

- Video-CoM: Interactive Video Reasoning via Chain of Manipulations (cs.CV; 2025-11-28)
  - Authors: Hanoona Rasheed; Mohammed Zumri; Muhammad Maaz; Ming-Hsuan Yang; Fahad Shahbaz Khan; Salman Khan
  - Problem: Most MLLMs “think about” videos in text space after a single encode, creating a semantic bottleneck; cannot rewatch/refocus/verify evidence.
  - Contributions:
    - New paradigm: Interactive Video Reasoning—models “think with videos” via a Chain of Manipulations (CoM), performing iterative visual actions.
    - Data/Training: Video-CoM Instruct (18K instruction-tuning set); reinforcement learning with reasoning-aware GRPO, adding step-level reasoning rewards beyond sparse answer rewards.
  - Results: Strong performance on 9 benchmarks; +3.6% average over recent SOTA while training on only ~25K SFT and 3K GRPO video samples; improved accuracy and interpretability.
  - Code: https://github.com/mbzuai-oryx/Video-CoM. PDF: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.23477v1

- Thinking by Doing: Building Efficient World Model Reasoning in LLMs via Multi-turn Interaction (cs.AI; 2025-11-28)
  - Authors: Bao Shu; Yan Cai; Jianjian Sun; Chunrui Han; En Yu; Liang Zhao; Jingcheng Hu; Yinmin Zhang; Haoran Lv; Yuang Peng; Zheng Ge; Xiangyu Zhang; Daxin Jiang; Xiangyu Yue
  - Problem: Rigid multi-turn reasoning limits active learning and efficient world-model internalization in LLM agents.
  - Contributions (WMAct):
    - Reward rescaling: ties outcome rewards to action efficacy to reduce redundancy and encourage purposeful interactions.
    - Interaction frequency annealing: progressively reduces allowed turns to force internalization of dynamics and reduce environment dependence.
  - Results: On Sokoban, Maze, Taxi, achieves single-turn solutions previously requiring multiple interactions; strong transfer to more complex environments; improved reasoning benchmarks.

