  - PBV association: Univariable protective both sexes; multivariable protective in males (aOR 1.30 per 100 cm3; 95% CI: 1.10–1.60), not females (aOR 1.10; 0.90–1.33).
  - Age effect: Each decade reduced independence odds by 30% in females (aOR 0.70; 0.62–0.79) vs 15% in males (aOR 0.85; 0.72–0.97; pinteraction=0.019). Age increased infarct size in females (+4.22 cm3/decade; p=0.033), not males.
  - Interpretation: Aging attenuates brain reserve in women; incorporate sex and PBV in outcome models.

