3) paper_id: 41237515
- Title: Artificial intelligence methods in gestational diabetes mellitus prediction: A systematic literature review.
- Authors: Ivanovic V et al.
- DOI: 10.1016/j.ijmedinf.2025.106158
- Published: 2026-01-01
- Study type: PRISMA-guided systematic review with dual quality assessment (PROBAST, IJMEDI)
- Scope: Databases (PubMed, Scopus, IEEE, Web of Science) to May 27, 2024; 78 studies on AI/ML predicting GDM using preconception and pregnancy data.
- Methods used (frequency): Logistic regression (46), tree-based models (41), support vector machines (29). Best-reported performers: neural networks (15), boosting (14), tree-based (13).
- Data aspects: 12 studies included preconception data.
- Reporting/validation: Sensitivity, specificity, calibration often underreported; decision-curve analysis rarely applied; 13 studies performed external validation.
- Trustworthiness: High risk of bias in most studies; IJMEDI indicated deficits in data preparation, validation, and deployment; few causal/explainable approaches.
- Recommendations: Prioritize transparent reporting, external validation, explainable/trustworthy models; leverage diverse longitudinal data; enhance collaboration among data scientists, clinicians, and healthcare systems.

