- Video-R2: Reinforcing Consistent and Grounded Reasoning in Multimodal Language Models (cs.CV)
  - Problem: Video reasoning traces in MLLMs can be logically inconsistent and weakly grounded in visual evidence.
  - Diagnostics: Introduces Think Answer Consistency (TAC) to measure alignment between reasoning and answers, and Video Attention Score (VAS) to quantify reliance on visual vs. textual cues. Analysis across 11 benchmarks shows heavy reliance on linguistic priors.
  - Method: Timestamp-aware supervised fine-tuning + Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) with a new Temporal Alignment Reward (TAR) to encourage temporally aligned, causally coherent video reasoning.
  - Results: Video-R2 improves TAC, VAS, and accuracy consistently across multiple video reasoning benchmarks. Code, dataset, and model to be open-sourced.

- Video-CoM: Interactive Video Reasoning via Chain of Manipulations (cs.CV)
  - Problem: Most MLLMs “think about videos” once and reason in text only; cannot rewatch/refocus/verify, causing shallow spatiotemporal reasoning.
  - Paradigm: “Think with videos” via a Chain of Manipulations (CoM) that performs iterative visual actions to gather/refine evidence.
  - Data/Training: Video-CoM Instruct (18K) for multi-step manipulation reasoning; RL with reasoning-aware GRPO using step-level reasoning rewards (beyond sparse answer rewards).
  - Efficiency/Results: Trained on 25K SFT + 3K GRPO samples; +3.6% average over recent SOTA across 9 benchmarks; improved accuracy and interpretability. Code: https://github.com/mbzuai-oryx/Video-CoM

- Thinking by Doing: Building Efficient World Model Reasoning in LLMs via Multi-turn Interaction (cs.AI)
  - Goal: Enable LLM agents to internalize world models efficiently through active interaction and reasoning (WMAct).
  - Mechanisms: Reward rescaling based on action efficacy to reduce redundancy; interaction frequency annealing to progressively cap interaction turns, pushing internalization of dynamics and single-turn solutions.
  - Results: On Sokoban, Maze, Taxi, WMAct solves tasks in one turn that previously needed multi-turn interaction; strong transfer and improved performance on reasoning benchmarks.

- AnyTalker: Scaling Multi-Person Talking Video Generation with Interactivity Refinement (cs.CV)
  - Challenge: Multi-person, audio-driven talking video generation is data-hungry and struggles with consistent multi-identity interactivity.
  - Architecture: Extensible multi-stream processing; identity-aware attention in Diffusion Transformer iteratively processes identity–audio pairs for scalable number of identities.
  - Training: Learns multi-person speaking patterns from single-person videos; refines interactivity with a small set of real multi-person clips.
  - Contributions/Results: New metric and dataset for interactivity; strong lip-sync, visual quality, and natural interactivity; favorable data cost vs. scalability trade-off.

- ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems (cs.LG; cs.CL)
  - Motivation: AlphaEvolve achieves new bounds with ensembles but is inference-only and closed-source.
  - Framework: Open-source single-LLM evolving system with large program database, batch sampling, lazy penalties to avoid stagnation, optional reward shaping; scales in-context learning and RL at test time.
  - Results: Small open-source model (DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B) achieves new best-known bounds on circle packing and first auto-correlation inequality from AlphaEvolve; test-time RL consistently outperforms inference-only; RL checkpoints learn evolving strategies and transfer to unseen tasks. Code: https://github.com/ypwang61/ThetaEvolve

