Tool `Paper Search:search_arxiv` with Parameter {'query': 'foundation models medicine 2024 survey', 'max_results': 10} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 4699 tokens): - Video-R2: Reinforcing Consistent and Grounded Reasoning in Multimodal Language Models (Maaz; Rasheed; Khan; Khan)
  - Problem: Video reasoning traces in MLLMs often sound plausible but are logically inconsistent or weakly grounded in visuals.
  - Diagnostics: Introduces Think Answer Consistency (TAC) for reasoning–answer alignment and Video Attention Score (VAS) for reliance on visual vs textual cues; analysis over 11 video reasoning benchmarks shows heavy dependence on linguistic priors.
  - Method: Dual-stage post-training—timestamp-aware supervised fine-tuning plus GRPO with a new Temporal Alignment Reward (TAR)—to enforce temporal precision and causal coherence.
  - Results: Consistently higher TAC, VAS, and accuracy across multiple benchmarks; code, dataset, and model to be open-sourced.

- Video-CoM: Interactive Video Reasoning via Chain of Manipulations (Rasheed; Zumri; Maaz; Yang; Khan; Khan)
  - Paradigm: “Think with videos” via Interactive Video Reasoning; model performs a Chain of Manipulations (CoM) to iteratively gather and refine visual evidence (rewatch, refocus, verify).
  - Data/Training: Video CoM Instruct (18K) for multi-step manipulation reasoning; RL with reasoning-aware GRPO using step-level reasoning rewards (beyond sparse answer rewards).
  - Results: Strong performance across 9 video reasoning benchmarks, +3.6% average over recent SOTA while training on only 25K SFT and 3K GRPO samples; improved accuracy and interpretability.
  - Code: https://github.com/mbzuai-oryx/Video-CoM

- Thinking by Doing: Building Efficient World Model Reasoning in LLMs via Multi-turn Interaction (Shu; Cai; Sun; Han; Yu; Zhao; Hu; Zhang; Lv; Peng; Ge; Zhang; Jiang; Yue)
  - Goal: Enable efficient world-model internalization through active interaction rather than rigid reasoning templates (WMAct).
  - Mechanisms: (1) Reward rescaling based on action efficacy to reduce redundancy and incentivize purposeful interaction; (2) Interaction frequency annealing to progressively reduce allowed turns, pushing internalization of dynamics.
  - Results: On Sokoban, Maze, Taxi, resolves tasks in a single turn that previously needed multiple interactions; strong transfer and improved performance on reasoning benchmarks.

- AnyTalker: Scaling Multi-Person Talking Video Generation with Interactivity Refinement (Zhong; Ji; Kong; Liu; Wang; Feng; Liu; Wang; Li; She; Qin; Li; Mao; Liu; Luo)
  - Architecture: Extensible multi-stream framework with identity-aware attention extending DiT blocks to iteratively process identity–audio pairs; scales to arbitrary numbers of identities.
  - Training: Learns multi-person speaking patterns from single-person videos; refines interactivity using only a few real multi-person clips.
  - Contributions: New metric and dataset targeting naturalness and interactivity evaluation.
  - Results: Strong lip-sync, visual quality, and natural interactivity; favorable trade-off between data cost and identity scalability.

- ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems (Wang; Su; Zeng; Xu; Ren; Yang; Huang; He; Ma; Peng; Cheng; He; Chen; Wang; Du; Shen)
  - Framework: Open-source evolution system enabling both in-context learning and RL at test time with a single LLM; supports continual learning on open optimization problems.
