  - Topic: Linked color imaging (LCI), an image-enhanced endoscopy modality that expands color differences, making reddish lesions more apparent and serrated lesions whiter.
  - Evidence: Eight RCTs; meta-analysis shows LCI superior to white-light endoscopy for detecting colorectal adenomatous lesions; improves serrated lesion detection and aids colonic mucosal assessment in ulcerative colitis.
