  - Multivariable: PBV protective in males (aOR 1.30 per 100 cm3; 1.10–1.60) but not in females (aOR 1.10; 0.90–1.33).
  - Each decade of age reduced independence odds more in females (aOR 0.70; 0.62–0.79) than males (0.85; 0.72–0.97); interaction p=0.019. Age associated with larger infarcts in females (+4.22 cm3/decade; p=0.033), not males.
  - Conclusion: Aging diminishes brain reserve benefits in women; include sex and PBV in outcome models.

- Concordance between IDSA Criteria for UTI Testing/Treating vs. ED Practice (doi:10.1101/2024.10.01.24314581)
