Tool `Paper Search:search_arxiv` with Parameter {'query': 'medical foundation models 2024 survey', 'max_results': 10} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 4699 tokens): Here are the key points for each paper:

1) Video-R2: Reinforcing Consistent and Grounded Reasoning in MLLMs
- Problem: Video reasoning traces in MLLMs can be logically inconsistent and weakly grounded in visuals, often relying on linguistic priors.
- Diagnostics: Introduces Think Answer Consistency (TAC) to assess alignment between reasoning and answers, and Video Attention Score (VAS) to quantify reliance on visual vs textual cues.
- Method: Two-stage post-training—timestamp-aware supervised fine-tuning plus Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) with a new Temporal Alignment Reward (TAR) to encourage temporally aligned, causally coherent reasoning.
- Results: Across 11 video reasoning benchmarks, improves TAC, VAS, and accuracy; better temporal precision and consistency lead to more trustworthy video understanding.
- Availability: Code, dataset, and model will be open-sourced.

2) Video-CoM: Interactive Video Reasoning via Chain of Manipulations
- Problem: Most MLLMs “think about” videos only after a single encoding, creating a semantic bottleneck.
- Paradigm: Interactive Video Reasoning—“think with videos” by iteratively manipulating the visual workspace.
- Model: Chain of Manipulations (CoM) executes visual actions to gather and refine evidence.
- Data: Video-CoM Instruct—18K instruction-tuning dataset for multi-step manipulation reasoning.
- Training: Supervised learning plus RL with reasoning-aware GRPO; introduces step-level reasoning rewards (not just sparse answer rewards) to improve grounding and consistency.
- Results: SOTA-level performance on 9 benchmarks, +3.6% average over recent SOTA while using only 25K SFT and 3K RL samples; improved accuracy and interpretability in ablations.
- Code: https://github.com/mbzuai-oryx/Video-CoM

3) Thinking by Doing (WMAct): Efficient World Model Reasoning in LLM Agents
- Problem: Rigid, over-structured reasoning during multi-turn interaction hinders active learning and efficient world model internalization.
- Method: WMAct removes rigid structure and builds reasoning through action with:
  - Reward rescaling based on action efficacy to reduce redundancy and encourage purposeful interaction.
  - Interaction frequency annealing to progressively reduce allowed turns, pushing internalization and less reliance on external feedback.
- Results: On Sokoban, Maze, Taxi, achieves single-turn resolutions for tasks previously requiring multiple interactions; demonstrates strong transferability and gains on reasoning benchmarks.

4) AnyTalker: Scaling Multi-Person Talking Video Generation
- Challenge: Data scarcity and coherent multi-identity interactivity in audio-driven multi-person video generation.
- Architecture: Extensible multi-stream Diffusion Transformer with identity-aware attention that iteratively processes identity–audio pairs; scales to arbitrary numbers of identities.
- Training: Primarily on single-person videos to learn speaking patterns; refine interactivity with a small set of real multi-person clips.
- Evaluation: New metric and dataset to assess naturalness and interactivity.
- Results: Strong lip sync, visual quality, and natural interactivity; balances data cost with identity scalability.

5) ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems
- Goal: Open-source framework extending AlphaEvolve to allow continual learning at test time via in-context learning and RL.
- Key components: Single LLM, large program database, batch sampling for throughput, lazy penalties against stagnation, optional reward shaping.
- Achievements: Enables small open-source model (DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B) to reach new best-known bounds on circle packing and the first auto-correlation inequality cited by AlphaEvolve.
- Findings: RL at test time consistently outperforms inference-only baselines; RL-trained checkpoints generalize faster and better on both trained and unseen tasks.
- Code: https://github.com/ypwang61/ThetaEvolve

