  Title: Predicting human tactile smoothness/roughness perception from multidimensional mechanical properties of synthetic fibers using machine learning.
  DOI: 10.1038/s41598-025-26294-5 | Published: 2025-01-01
  Objective: Build a predictive model of human smoothness/roughness perception using multidimensional mechanical properties of synthetic fibers.
  Data/Methods: 50 commercially available fiber samples (polyester, spandex, nylon, blends). Measured 12 mechanical properties across 4 categories (geometric roughness, frictional force, hardness, tensile strength). 37 participants rated tactile smoothness/roughness on a 5-point scale (lower = smoother, higher = rougher). Correlation analysis and six regression models evaluated; Gaussian process regression (GPR) performed best (highest cross-validated accuracy).
