  - Key findings: Abstract indicates successful model development and testing; specific performance metrics not reported.

- CT-based intratumoral heterogeneity + deep learning radiomics for LNM in early-stage LUAD (PubMed 41298638; Sci Rep; doi: 10.1038/s41598-025-26331-3; 2025-01-01)
  - Objective: Quantify CT-based intratumoral heterogeneity (ITH) and fuse with deep learning radiomics to predict lymph node metastasis (LNM) in early-stage lung adenocarcinoma.
  - Data/Design: Multicenter retrospective cohort, 787 surgical LUAD patients across three centers.
  - Methods: Unsupervised clustering of 2D CT tumor subregions to derive an ITHscore; fusion model integrating deep learning features, Radscore, and ITHscore.
  - Results: ITHscore was an important predictor; fusion model achieved AUCs of 0.813, 0.807, 0.718 in test sets; gene set enrichment in a test subset showed epithelial–mesenchymal transition as top enriched signature (NES = 1.71), supporting biological plausibility.
  - Implication: Fused imaging heterogeneity with DL features improves LNM prediction; supports translational relevance.

