1) Application of Narrative and AI-Assisted Follow-Up After Voluntary Medical Male Circumcision: Multicenter, Double-Blind, Prospective, Randomized Controlled Trial.
- Authors: Wang L et al.
- DOI: 10.2196/68573 | Pub date: 2025-01-01 | Source/URL: PubMed https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41248462/
- Aim: Address postoperative anxiety and adherence challenges after VMMC by testing narrative-based interventions and LLM-enabled automated follow-up.
- Rationale: Telemedicine access and communication gaps hinder recovery; narrative approaches reduce distress in other settings; LLMs may enable scalable follow-up.
- Design: Multicenter, double-blind, prospective RCT.
- Outcomes: Not reported in abstract; study explores feasibility/efficacy of narrative + AI-assisted care in VMMC.

2) MoveMentor—examining the effectiveness of a machine learning and app-based digital assistant to increase physical activity in adults: protocol for a randomised controlled trial.
- Authors: Vandelanotte C et al.
- DOI: 10.1186/s13063-025-08926-3 | Pub date: 2025-01-01 | URL: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40597442/
- Aim: Evaluate whether an ML-driven, app-based digital assistant using real-time data increases physical activity.
- Rationale: Physical inactivity is prevalent; scalable interventions often have modest effects and engagement; ML personalization may improve outcomes.
- Design: RCT protocol (no results yet).

