- Context: Digital health technologies (DHTs) can enhance clinical trials and inclusivity, but generalizability and translation to practice are challenging.
- Aim: Leverage LLMs to scale evidence harvesting on DHT-enabled RCTs.
- Methods: Developed three LLM tasks for automated title screening and information extraction across multiple models.
- Findings: Promising performance for large-scale literature review acceleration toward equity/inclusion aims.

5) An Intervention to Increase Advance Care Planning Among Older Adults With Advanced Cancer: A Randomized Clinical Trial.
- Authors: Volandes AE et al.
- DOI: 10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2025.9150 | Pub date: 2025-01-01 | URL: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40343696/
- Problem: Many older adults with advanced cancer do not communicate goals of care/preferences; care may not align with values.
- Aim: Test a scalable model to increase advance care planning (ACP).
- Design: Randomized clinical trial (details/results not reported in abstract).

6) A vaccine chatbot intervention for parents to improve HPV vaccination uptake among middle school girls: a cluster randomized trial.
