Tool `Paper Search:search_pubmed` with Parameter {'query': 'ClinVar 2023 update Nucleic Acids Research', 'max_results': 10} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 1830 tokens): - RMVar 2.0: Updated database of functional variants in RNA modifications (RMs) for human disease research. Key advances: an enhanced analytical pipeline applied to the latest RM datasets and genetic variants; first-time incorporation of allele-specific RNA modification analysis to identify RM-associated variants (not present in RMVar 1.0 or similar resources); extensive annotations covering RNA-binding protein interactions, RNA-RNA interactions, splicing events, and circular RNAs to investigate post-transcriptional regulation; integrated disease-related information from ClinVar and GWAS. Access: http://rmvar.renlab.cn. DOI: 10.1093/nar/gkae924. Published: 2025-01-01.

- DIANA-microT 2023: Latest release of DIANA-microT-CDS, a miRNA target prediction algorithm identifying binding sites in both 3′UTRs and coding sequences with high performance. Updated interactions generated using Ensembl v102, miRBase 22.1, and (for the first time) MirGeneDB 2.1, yielding >83 million predicted interactions across human, mouse, rat, chicken, fly, and worm. New: predicted interactions for miRNAs encoded by 20 viruses against host transcripts (human, mouse, chicken). Integrates DIANA-TarBase, plasmiR, HMDD, UCSC, dbSNP, ClinVar, plus miRNA/gene abundance for 369 cell lines/tissues. Redesigned interface with smart filters, abundance pattern discovery, SNP-in-binding-site pinpointing, and miRNA–disease links. Freely accessible and downloadable without login: www.microrna.gr/microt_webserver/. DOI: 10.1093/nar/gkad283. Published: 2023-01-01.

- NCBI database resources (2023): Overview of NCBI’s 35+ databases and services (e.g., GenBank, PubMed) with programmatic access via E-utilities. New resources: Comparative Genome Resource (CGR) and BLAST ClusteredNR. Major updates: PubMed, PMC, Bookshelf, IgBLAST, Genome Data Viewer (GDV), RefSeq, NCBI Virus, GenBank type assemblies, iCn3D, ClinVar, GTR, dbGaP, ALFA, ClinicalTrials.gov, Pathogen Detection, antimicrobial resistance resources, and PubChem. Access: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov. DOI: 10.1093/nar/gkac1032. Published: 2023-01-01.

- The new uORFdb: Central hub for upstream ORF (uORF) research integrating literature, sequence, and variation data. uORFs (initiated by AUG or near-cognate codons) regulate downstream translation and can produce non-canonical peptides; mutations are linked to disease including cancer. The updated sequence-based uORFdb provides sequence data, graphical displays, and variant information for >2.4 million human uORFs and >4.2 million uORFs across 12 additional species. Features: visualization of multiple uORFs in transcript- and reading-frame-specific contexts; rich filters; links to UCSC Genome Browser, dbSNP, and ClinVar; inclusion of uORF-related somatic variation from WGS of 677 TCGA cancer samples. Access: https://www.bioinformatics.uni-muenster.de/tools/uorfdb. DOI: 10.1093/nar/gkac899. Published: 2023-01-01.
