 Sharon E; Streicher H; Li S; McShane LM; Rubinstein L; Patton DR; Williams PM; Coffey B; Hamilton SR; Bahary N; Suga JM; Hatoum H; Abrams JS; Conley BA; Arteaga CL; Harris L; O'Dwyer PJ; Chen AP; Flaherty KT","abstract":"The National Cancer Institute Molecular Analysis for Therapy Choice (NCI-MATCH) trial, the largest national precision oncology study to date (> 1,100 sites) of patients with relapsed or refractory malignancies, assigned patients to targeted therapy in parallel phase II studies based on tumor molecular alterations. The anti-programmed death receptor 1 inhibitor nivolumab previously showed activity in mismatch repair (MMR)-deficient colon cancer. We hypothesized that nivolumab would have activity in patients with MMR-deficient, noncolorectal tumors.","doi":"10.1200/JCO.19.00818","published_date":"2020-01-01T00:00:00","pdf_url":"","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31765263/","source":"pubmed","updated_date":"2020-01-01T00:00:00","categories":"","keywords":"","citations":0,"references":"","extra":""}]
