  - Perspective/commentary on the role of artificial intelligence in conducting literature reviews in oncology.
  - Discusses opportunities, challenges, and evolving standards for integrating AI into evidence synthesis.

- Standardizing Time-to-Event Reporting in Single-Arm BCG-Unresponsive Registration Trials: A Case for Kaplan-Meier (DOI: 10.1016/j.annonc.2025.11.010; 2025-01-01)
  - Methodology piece advocating for Kaplan–Meier-based time-to-event reporting in single-arm registration trials for BCG-unresponsive bladder cancer.
  - Aims to improve consistency, interpretability, and regulatory alignment of outcome reporting.

- ROME trial Wasn't Built in a Day: The Decade-Long Journey to Randomized Evidence in Precision Oncology (DOI: 10.1016/j.annonc.2025.11.016; 2025-01-01)
  - Commentary on the ROME trial and the protracted path to generating randomized evidence in precision oncology.
  - Highlights lessons learned, methodological hurdles, and implications for future targeted trial designs.

- Sacituzumab Tirumotecan in Participants With Advanced or Metastatic Urothelial Carcinoma and Disease Progression after Chemotherapy and Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors (DOI: 10.1016/j.annonc.2025.11.013; 2025-01-01)
  - Phase 1/2 (2870-001/KL264-01, cohort 9) preliminary results of sacituzumab tirumotecan (sac-TMT) monotherapy in advanced/metastatic urothelial carcinoma after progression on chemotherapy and immune checkpoint inhibitors.
  - Sac-TMT is a TROP2-directed antibody–drug conjugate with a unique bifunctional linker designed to maximize payload delivery; early data reported.

- Kinetics and determinants of ESR1 mutation detection in metastatic breast cancer (DOI: 10.1016/j.annonc.2025.11.002; 2025-01-01)
  - Builds on PADA-1, the first prospective randomized trial showing benefit of early therapeutic targeting of blood-detected ESR1 mutations (bESR1).
  - Examines temporal dynamics and factors influencing ESR1 mutation detection in metastatic breast cancer, informing monitoring and treatment adaptation.

- Pooled analysis by best confirmed response to trastuzumab deruxtecan and related biomarkers in patients with HER2-positive metastatic breast cancer from DESTINY-Breast01, DESTINY-Breast02, and DESTINY-Breast03 (DOI: 10.1016/j.annonc.2025.11.007; 2025-01-01)
  - Integrates data across three trials of trastuzumab deruxtecan (T-DXd) in HER2-positive metastatic breast cancer, stratified by best confirmed response and linked biomarkers.
  - Prior reported objective response rates were 62% (DB-01), 70% (DB-02), and 79% (DB-03); pooled analysis explores correlates of response and resistance.

- ESMO Basic Requirements for AI-based Biomarkers In Oncology (EBAI) (DOI: 10.1016/j.annonc.2025.11.009; 2025-01-01)
  - Consensus recommendations defining foundational requirements for AI-based biomarkers suitable for routine oncology practice.
  - Addresses methodological standards, validation, clinical utility, interpretability, data governance, and multidisciplinary collaboration to bridge oncology and computer science.

- Association between type and location of germline BRCA1/2 pathogenic or likely pathogenic variants with phenotype and prognosis in young patients with breast cancer: results from an international cohort study (DOI: 10.1016/j.annonc.2025.11.004; 2025-01-01)
  - International cohort study assessing how specific types and genomic locations of germline BRCA1/2 pathogenic/likely pathogenic variants relate to clinical phenotype and prognosis in young breast cancer patients.
  - Seeks to refine risk stratification and management based on variant-level granularity.

