Tool `NASA Data:get_coronal_mass_ejection` with Parameter {'start_date': '2025-11-27', 'end_date': '2025-12-02'} on NASA Data succeeded. Result (summarized from 1664 tokens): Summary of reported CMEs (total found: 31; detailed entries below cover those provided; remaining 21 not detailed in the source excerpt)

Overall patterns (2025-11-27 to 2025-11-28):
- Geometry/instruments: Most CMEs were observed to the NE/NNE/E in SOHO LASCO C2/C3, STEREO-A COR2, and GOES CCOR-1; sources often indicated in GOES SUVI 284/304. Multiple SOHO LASCO real-time data gaps limited coverage.
- Sources: Predominantly beyond or just over the NE limb (far-sided/near-limb), including continuous outflow and a large NE-quadrant filament eruption; one event associated with faint post-eruptive arcades near N45E65.
- Speeds/types: Analysis speeds range ~267–685 km/s; majority Type S, with two Type C in the listed subset.
- Overlap: Several CMEs overlapped in time/space, particularly those tied to the NE-quadrant filament eruption.

Detailed entries (as provided)

1) ID: 2025-11-27T00:00:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T00:00Z
- Obs: First seen NE by LASCO C2; also LASCO C3, STEREO-A COR2, GOES CCOR-1 later.
- Source: No clear source; likely far-sided.
- Analysis: 2025-11-27T09:22Z; 379 km/s; Type S.
- Link: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/43031/-1

2) ID: 2025-11-27T02:24:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T02:24Z
- Obs: Bright, narrow NE CMEs in LASCO C2/C3, GOES CCOR-1; NE in STEREO-A COR2.
- Source: Continued outflow from on/just beyond NE limb; SUVI 284/304 shows successive opening field lines/partial filament liftoffs over hours.
- Analysis: 2025-11-27T11:10Z; 414 km/s; Type S.
- Link: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/43045/-1

3) ID: 2025-11-27T04:24:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T04:24Z
- Obs: Narrow flux-rope CME NE in LASCO C2/C3, GOES CCOR-1; NE in STEREO-A COR2.
- Source: Part of continuous NE-limb outflow; very subtle rising loop beyond NE limb in SUVI 284 at ~03:52Z.
- Analysis: 2025-11-27T14:57Z; 327 km/s; Type S.
- Link: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/43048/-1

4) ID: 2025-11-27T08:48:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T08:48Z
- Obs: NE in LASCO C2 and GOES CCOR-1; NE in STEREO-A COR2.
- Source: Faint rising loop beyond NNE limb seen in SUVI 284 starting ~07:24Z.
- Notes: LASCO C2/C3 captured only a few real-time frames due to scheduled data gap.
- Analysis: 2025-11-27T22:04Z; 299 km/s; Type S.
- Link: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/43052/-1

5) ID: 2025-11-27T13:53:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T13:53Z
- Obs: NNE in STEREO-A COR2 and GOES CCOR-1; overlapped with two preceding CMEs.
- Source: Likely widely opening field lines beyond NNE limb; SUVI 284 shows onset ~12:48Z; SUVI 304 shows very subtle beyond-limb motion.
- Notes: Not captured in LASCO C2/C3 real time due to data gap.
- Analysis: 2025-11-27T18:39Z; 685 km/s; Type C.
- Link: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/43054/-1

6) ID: 2025-11-27T18:45:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T18:45Z
- Obs: First seen E in GOES CCOR-1; small portion in STEREO-A COR2.
- Source candidates: (1) NE-limb filament spanning most of NE quadrant, erupting as early as ~16:00Z in SUVI 304; (2) eruption near E limb starting ~17:16Z in SUVI 304; CCOR-1 front may be a combination.
- Analysis: 2025-11-28T01:04Z; 489 km/s; Type S.
- Link: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/43059/-1

7) ID: 2025-11-27T20:23:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T20:23Z
- Obs: First seen NE in STEREO-A COR2; also NE in GOES CCOR-1; LASCO C2/C3 covered by real-time data gap.
- Source: Most likely part of the NE-limb filament eruption (spanning NE quadrant; activity from ~16:00Z); partially overlaps the back of the 18:45Z CME.
- Analysis: 2025-11-28T09:41Z; 267 km/s; Type S.
- Link: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/43061/-1

8) ID: 2025-11-27T23:45:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T23:45Z
- Obs: Faint CME to E in GOES CCOR-1; STEREO-A COR2 and LASCO C2/C3 had real-time data gaps.
- Source: Eruption on/near E limb; ejecta leaving E limb in SUVI 304 starting ~22:32Z.
- Notes: Fades before reaching CCOR-1 FO
